---
import { DOCS_URL, STARTER_URL } from "../lib/site";
---
<section class="m-section" id="self-hosting" aria-labelledby="hosting-title"><div class="m-split">
 <div><div class="m-eyebrow">Self-host your blog frontend</div><h2 class="m-title" id="hosting-title">Your website.<br/>Your server.<br/><em>Your choice.</em></h2><p class="m-copy">Run your blog pages wherever you run your website. Use the Next.js starter on your own Node.js server, deploy it on Cloudflare, or build with the public JavaScript SDK.</p><p class="m-copy">The frontend is yours to host and edit. BlogStack Cloud handles the publishing dashboard, API, media and AI behind it.</p><div class="m-actions"><a class="m-button" href={DOCS_URL+"/docs/self-hosting"}>Read the self-hosting guide</a><a class="m-link" href={STARTER_URL}>Download the starter</a></div></div>
 <div class="m-shell"><div class="m-panel hosting-recipe"><div class="recipe-header">A small setup. A complete blog.</div><pre><span>Install the starter</span>
npm install

<span>Set three public configuration values</span>
BLOGSTACK_PROJECT_SLUG=my-blog
BLOGSTACK_API_URL=https://blogstack-app.hidden-silence-2d18.workers.dev
SITE_URL=https://yourwebsite.com

<span>Build and run on your server</span>
npm run build
npm run start</pre><div class="recipe-footer"><span>MIT components</span><span>No private API key for public pages</span></div></div></div>
</div></section>
<style>.recipe-header{font-size:.9rem;padding:22px 26px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06)}pre{padding:26px;font:400 .78rem/1.9 var(--mono);white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;color:#d7d7dc}pre span{color:var(--text-muted);display:inline-block;margin-bottom:4px}.recipe-footer{padding:18px 26px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 22px;font-size:.72rem;color:var(--text-muted);background:rgba(255,255,255,.018)}@media(max-width:480px){pre{padding:20px;font-size:.72rem}.recipe-header{padding:20px}}</style>
